most people never realize their dreams  they never get the car they want start  the business they want make the money  they want because most people are so  busy being afraid that they never take  their shot at a real life most people  choose their path out of fear disguised  as practicality you do the smart thing  the safe thing you go to school that  you're supposed to you get a job like  you're supposed to you get married and  have kids like you're supposed to who  the heck is setting up all these rules  for your life who are these people  telling you what you can and cannot do  and more importantly why are you  listening to them have your parents  accomplish what you want to accomplish  has your guidance counselor done what  you want to do even though what they  tell you that you should do is that out  of love how can they advise you when  they've never gone where you want to go  why do you let their limited view of the  world hold you back from doing something  great I want you right now to pause and  take a look at your life look at your  friends look at your family look at the  books you read the videos you watch and  the media you consume you have hidden  talents that you're not using because  your environment is holding you where  you are you might watch a motivational  video attend a seminar  read an inspiring book and have a brief  moment of boldness a moment where you  believe in yourself a moment where you  believe that your dreams are possible a  moment where you believe that your  talents are valuable and the next day  you wake up and you're right back to  where you started because BAM your  environment smashes you back to where  you were you need to decide whether  you're going to live your life or  someone else's version of your life find  that hidden talent of yours and nurture  it believe in it pursue it relentlessly  stop listening to the doubters the  haters and the naysayers if someone  hasn't done what you want to do their  advice is meaningless  who are they to counsel you if anything  you should do the exact opposite of what  they say because you don't want a life  like theirs if you want a great life  then you need to do something that you  are great at that's always the start  trust your heart not your head and  follow your passion it will lead you to  places that your head cannot contemplate  you need to have an illogical irrational  irrevocable love for what you're doing  you need to embrace your hidden talent  and show the world what you can do then  change your environment to cultivate an  aura of greatness surround yourself with  people ideas and resources that push you  to stretch your comfort zone and become  the best version of yourself eject the  deadweight and negativity from your life  create a morning routine and ritual to  start your day off inspired and  motivated not just every now and then  but every single day inspired and  motivated you have an important mission  to accomplish and every day you waste is  one last day you have to make your  dreams happen now I don't know what your  hidden talent is but I know it's  powerful it's something you can change  the world with and you can either  believe that but believe what all the  underachievers around you think it's  time to start living your version of  your life no more excuses
 

